&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Fullstack Web Developer to join our Web Apps team, in our Zürich office. In this role you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The web apps team plays a central role at Auterion and owns the systems that add connectivity and remote interfaces for fleet management and operations. Our services are responsible for ingesting and analyzing flight telemetry data, managing and updating the fleet as well as integrating with other systems across the stack.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across all the team’s web based projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate services between edge devices and our centralized services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle new feature discovery, prototyping and investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Customer Success team in debugging and resolving customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze user usage patterns and other statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push initiatives to clean up, upgrade, and refactor existing services to reduce technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve integrations with 3rd party services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a Fullstack web development or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Node.js&amp;nbsp; ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Typescript ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with modern SPAs (Vue.js ecosystem preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Postgres/SQL (queries, transactions, views, indexes, triggers) as well as ORM systems (Prisma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Docker and container orchestration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with CI/CD pipelines (GoCD and GH Actions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monitoring and observability tools (Datadog, Grafana)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python proficiency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CH/EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Buyer domain&#39;s Data Science teams build and iterate on our most critical ML systems—like ranking, retrieval, and recommendations—that serve millions of users. As our ambition and the complexity of these models grow, we are scaling our MLOps capabilities to match:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring an MLOps Engineer to solve this. This is a high-impact &quot;bridge&quot; role, not to build new platforms, but to be the expert user of our existing platforms (GCP/Vertex AI, Vespa, Triton). Your mission is to take our Data Science team&#39;s work, rectify the current ad-hoc solutions, and build the robust, automated, and high-quality &quot;path-to-production&quot; our advanced models require.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also by joining Vinted, you’ll become part of an active community of engineers who are keen on sharing knowledge, organizing learning workshops and so much more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Productionise ML models: &lt;/strong&gt;be responsible for migrating all existing model training code from experimental or proof-of-concept stages to robust and automated pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build continuous training (CT) pipelines: &lt;/strong&gt;design, build, and maintain automated workflows for data preparation, model training, and batch scoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate model serving &amp;amp; integration: &lt;/strong&gt;package and deploy traditional ML models (e.g., in ONNX format) to our existing serving infrastructure, primarily Vespa and/or Triton.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the deployment loop: &lt;/strong&gt;automate model deployments where they are still manual. For example, building a GitHub Action that deploys a new model to Vespa, triggered by a webhook from a successful Vertex AI training pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the missing quality gates: &lt;/strong&gt;build the automated quality and evaluation gates that our pipelines lack today. This includes:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish and uphold ML Model Lifecycle Standards: &lt;/strong&gt;Take ownership of and continuously improve the standards, quality, and governance of the complete ML model lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are looking for an &quot;ML-literate&quot; Software Engineer, not a Data Scientist. You are a builder and an automator with a strong service mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must-have technical skills: deep expertise in GCP/Vertex AI (or equivalents like SageMaker), Kubernetes, and Docker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation expertise: proven experience building robust CI/CD and automation pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions, Jenkins, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ML-Literate: you understand ML workflows and concepts (training, evaluation, inference) well enough to debug pipelines and build meaningful quality gates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soft skills: a strong &quot;service mindset,&quot; excellent communication, and the ability to act as a bridge between the highly technical worlds of Data Science and Infrastructure. You are pragmatic and driven to get high-quality work into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus Points: familiarity with ML serving platforms like Vespa search engine or NVIDIA Triton and model formats like ONNX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn and master new technologies and concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We value pragmatism, big-picture thinking, curiosity, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A daily lunch allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An NS mobility card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;JobsDescription_sectionContent__jYQtX&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€89.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€121.400 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help protect what truly matters in our customers&#39; most critical environments by proactively identifying threats and improving how they are detected and addressed.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission Critical Security Engineer with a focus on Threat Hunting, you will be part of a dedicated customer team responsible for securing and continuously improving a complex, mission-critical application landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working alongside other engineers and security specialists, you will help ensure the environment remains as secure and resilient as possible. You combine a strong engineering foundation with a security mindset, taking ownership of security improvements and understanding how systems, applications, and infrastructure behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your specific focus will be on threat hunting and detection engineering. Using your in-depth knowledge of the customer&#39;s technology stack and application landscape, you will fine-tune existing detection use cases and develop new ones tailored to the environment. You will use our custom SIEM/SOAR-based Managed Detection and Response (MDR) platform to turn emerging threats and technical insights into actionable detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role bridges security engineering, detection engineering, and threat intelligence. You don&#39;t simply follow predefined playbooks. You understand system behavior, identify gaps, and develop practical solutions that strengthen the security of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat intelligence &amp;amp; continuous improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actively follow security developments, vulnerabilities, and threat intelligence and translate these into relevant hunts and detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify security risks and gaps in detection coverage and proactively propose improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your knowledge of the customer&#39;s application and infrastructure landscape to continuously strengthen its security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the evolution of the team&#39;s security monitoring and detection strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate findings into clear, actionable communication for engineers, customer stakeholders, and security specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to security advisories and share relevant threats across the customer team and wider organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with engineers to understand system behavior and validate detection strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with the customer&#39;s Security Operations Center (SOC) to align security monitoring, threat detection, and response activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help establish and improve integrations with the customer&#39;s SIEM/SOAR platform, including the forwarding of relevant logs and security telemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection engineering &amp;amp; threat hunting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and continuously improve detection use cases based on emerging threats and observed behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate threat scenarios and security insights into actionable detection logic tailored to the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proactively perform threat hunting across the application and infrastructure landscape to identify abnormal or suspicious patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analyze logs and telemetry data to uncover behaviors that are not yet covered by existing detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your understanding of the customer&#39;s technology stack to distinguish normal from potentially malicious behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use case development &amp;amp; response design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define what should happen when detections trigger, including response actions, automation, and escalation paths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuously refine detection logic to improve quality, relevance, and signal-to-noise ratio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and fine-tune custom detection scenarios based on the specific characteristics and security requirements of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage our custom SIEM/SOAR-based MDR platform to implement detections and analyze data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with platform and automation engineers to improve integrations and detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply engineering and automation practices to ensure detection solutions are scalable, reliable, and maintainable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines solid engineering fundamentals with a strong interest in security and is motivated to move towards or deepen their expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t necessarily need to be an experienced threat hunter already. What matters is your ability to understand complex systems, recognize unusual behavior, and translate technical insights into practical security improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid engineering fundamentals, including Linux, networking, and infrastructure behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, or similar platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with CI/CD, Git, and configuration management or infrastructure-as-code tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong automation mindset and the ability to translate problems into scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with logs and telemetry to analyze system behavior and investigate technical issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Python and/or Bash scripting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with SIEM or log analytics platforms such as OpenSearch, Elastic, Splunk, or Microsoft Sentinel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of security principles, including threat detection and response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to distinguish normal from abnormal system behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analytical, curious, and driven to understand how systems and threats behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ownership mindset, with responsibility for security quality and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication skills to translate technical findings into actionable insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to connect business and customer context to technical security solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with threat hunting, detection engineering, or advanced SOC operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience developing or improving detection use cases and security monitoring rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with SOAR or security automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep knowledge of Microsoft Entra ID, Azure, and other Microsoft cloud services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with threat intelligence frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience integrating SIEM/SOAR platforms or forwarding security telemetry between different environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ Who are you?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an engineer with a strong interest in security, driven to understand how systems behave and how threats manifest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t follow playbooks blindly. You want to understand why detections exist, how systems interact, and where security can be improved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You combine analytical thinking with a hands-on mindset and enjoy working with complex applications, infrastructure, and data. You are curious, proactive, and take ownership of the quality of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also enjoy being part of a customer team where security is a shared responsibility. You work closely with fellow engineers and security specialists, communicate clearly with stakeholders, and contribute to keeping the entire environment secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What can you expect?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis, you&#39;ll join a community of engineers with an awesome combination of exceptionally high security standards, an infatuation with automation, and the power to make a positive, sustainable impact on customers&#39; business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work within a dedicated customer team where engineers and security specialists jointly take responsibility for the security and reliability of mission-critical environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of our customer engagements, there is no pressure on (billable) hours; we focus on quality and impact or how we like to call it:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;freedom &amp;amp; responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;. You know best how to deliver the most value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be embedded in a company committed to helping colleagues grow as people and professionals through training, knowledge sharing, mentoring, and good old-fashioned fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are high-quality workspaces, and we go way beyond what is expected. We have productive equipment, good food and drinks, team outings, family days, labs to experiment with innovative technologies, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re active in relevant tech communities, attending and organizing meetups and conferences, and we organize internal knowledge-sharing events where Tech Leads play an important role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re an engineer in the Netherlands with a strong interest in security and want to help secure mission-critical environments while developing or deepening your expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h6&gt;Every order a Suitsupply customer places, online, in a store, or through customer service, has to be captured, understood and carried all the way through to delivery or return. As Junior Product Manager for IT Fulfillment, you will help build and improve the services that make that happen: the order flows, data and interfaces that connect our webstore, our stores, our warehouses and our customer service teams.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;You will work in a small team inside the IT Fulfillment domain, alongside the Group Product Manager and our own engineers. The Group Product Manager shapes the functional direction with the business and sets priorities; together you turn it into clear requirements, well-defined tickets and working software, built with engineers and AI agents. This is a technical product role: we build our own services, so you will spend your time in data models, interfaces and requirements rather than managing a vendor’s roadmap. You start close to delivery, with support while you learn the domain, and grow into owning more of the roadmap.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn mapped-out functional flows into clear, buildable work: technical requirements, acceptance criteria and user stories that engineers and AI agents can pick up without coming back with questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the detail as both product manager and business analyst: the data model, the way systems talk to each other, and the edge cases nobody thought of yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break large changes into chunks that can be built, tested and released safely, and keep the backlog in a state where work can start at any moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers day to day in refinement, planning, reviews and releases, and use our AI tooling to draft, structure and pressure-test the work before it reaches them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design our order data and interfaces so that AI agents can read, reason over and act on them as reliably as our own systems do.&lt;/li&gt;
